    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Cut two deep slashes to the bone on each leg quarter, one through the thigh and one through the drumstick, so the marinade gets in.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Mix the lemongrass, ginger, garlic, vinegar, calamansi juice, sugar, salt and pepper in a bowl. Add the chicken, rub the marinade into the slashes, cover and refrigerate.",
        "minutes": 120
      },
      {
        "text": "Make the basting oil: warm the oil and annatto seeds in a small pan over low heat, stirring, until the oil turns deep orange-red. Do not let the seeds smoke. Strain, discard the seeds and stir in the butter, salt and calamansi juice.",
        "minutes": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Light a charcoal grill and let the coals burn down to a steady medium heat covered in white ash. Oil the grate.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Lift the chicken out of the marinade and brush off the bits of lemongrass and garlic, which burn on the grill. Grill, turning every 5 minutes and brushing with basting oil each time, until the skin is charred in spots and the juices at the bone run clear, or the thickest part reads 165°F (74°C).",
        "minutes": 35
      },
      {
        "text": "Stir the soy sauce, calamansi juice and chili together for the dip.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Rest the chicken for 5 minutes, brush once more with basting oil and serve with rice, extra basting oil and the dip.",
        "minutes": 5
      }
    ],
    "tips": "For deeper flavor, marinate overnight. No grill? Roast on a rack at 400°F (200°C) for 35 to 40 minutes, basting twice, then broil for 3 minutes to char the skin."
